---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BlockLink from "../../components/BlockLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
    This Privacy Policy describes how the Poker Tritons Floor Bot ("the Bot") collects, uses, and stores information when operating within the Poker Tritons Discord server at UC San Diego.
    </p>

    <p>
    By using the Bot, you agree to the collection and use of information as described in this policy.
    </p>

    <p>Information collected by the Bot may include:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>Discord user ID, username, and server-related identifiers.</li>
    <li>UC San Diego email address provided for verification.</li>
    <li>Email verification status (verified or unverified).</li>
    <li>Ledger and transaction records related to poker games and club activity.</li>
    <li>Payment confirmation data submitted through the Bot.</li>
    <li>Command usage data necessary for Bot functionality and auditing.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>How this information is used:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>To verify UC San Diego affiliation via email verification.</li>
    <li>To manage tables, ledgers, and player balances.</li>
    <li>To support payment tracking and verification processes.</li>
    <li>To enforce host accountability and maintain accurate records.</li>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and improve Bot functionality.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Data storage and retention:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>Data is stored only as long as necessary to support club operations.</li>
    <li>Ledger and transaction data may be retained for historical accuracy and dispute resolution.</li>
    <li>Email verification status may be retained to prevent repeated verification.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Data sharing:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>Data is not sold or shared with third parties for commercial purposes.</li>
    <li>Information may be accessible to authorized Poker Tritons administrators for moderation and operational purposes.</li>
    <li>Data may be disclosed if required to comply with applicable laws or enforce server rules.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Security:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>Reasonable measures are taken to protect stored data.</li>
    <li>No system can guarantee absolute security.</li>
    <li>Users are responsible for maintaining the security of their Discord accounts.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>User rights and responsibility:</p>

    <ul>
    <li>Users should only submit information they are authorized to provide, including UC San Diego email addresses they own.</li>
    <li>Users may request removal or correction of their data by contacting server administrators.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
    The Bot may rely on third-party services such as Discord and email verification providers. Their data handling practices are governed by their respective privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated at any time. Continued use of the Bot after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>
</BaseLayout>